Fail fast when the network is unreachable

Offline launches waited minutes in the runtime: every request retried three
times on connect failures and each attempt ran into Wine's unbounded name
resolution and 20-second connect default, and the sign-in thread then made a
delayed second round. Requests now bound resolution and connect to 5 seconds
each, stop retrying on name-resolution, connect, timeout and connection
errors (server errors are still retried), and the sign-in falls back to the
cached identity after the first unreachable attempt. With
XODUS_FORCE_OFFLINE=1 the cached sign-in completes at once; the
offline-identity contract probe checks both paths finish within two seconds.

